From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: knapcio <knapcio@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 09:31:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 31/31] S2: steer the MoE shared-expert finalize in batched
 decode steps (shared-scope profiles)

s2_layer bound each S2 layer with make_layer, whose K1 arguments start zeroed, and did not copy the shared-scope
steering fields that layer_base sets. With a shared-scope profile, decode steps shared by two or more sessions therefore
skipped the shared-expert correction on every steered MoE layer; attention and dense-MLP steering were applied, and solo
decode and prefill were fully steered (kindlingai/gr8#196).

- k1_steer: one helper sets the finalize steering for layer_base and s2_layer. base_bind / s2_bind hold the binding
  steps after make_layer (same code, same order); s2_bind refuses a binding whose steering differs from today's layer
  of the same M.
- Runtime signature " s2steer 1" with a shared-scope profile; boot receipt "steering S2: X of Y S2 MoE layer bindings
  ..." per rank.
- s2_steer_test: the production bindings, and S2 rows of the shared finalize and the attention consume against each
  session's and each row's own launch, byte for byte. Built by scripts/build.sh with the other steering fixtures and by
  scripts/c1_tests.sh (EXTRA=-DDEC_S2).

Steering off: no change to the K1 arguments, the signature or the device code.
